    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. There's only one test class (`AcceptanceTest`) in the project, and it passes along with everything else.\n\n## Summary\n\nTo make owner creation return `displayName` formatted as `LastName, FirstName`, I made two changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `displayName` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` includes the field in API responses.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto(...)` that computes `displayName` as `owner.getLastName() + \", \" + owner.getFirstName()` from the stored names.\n\nSince the controller already maps the saved `Owner` through `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(...)` on both create (`POST /api/owners`) and read (`GET /api/owners/{id}`), the derived `displayName` is now returned consistently. The acceptance test `coreComputesDisplayName` and the full build pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).",
